    "created_at": "2025-07-01T20:39:20Z",
    "updated_at": "2025-07-01T20:40:14Z",
    "body": "RFC 6265bis actually does instruct how to handle empty Path strings: https://datatracker.ietf.org/doc/html/draft-ietf-httpbis-rfc6265bis#name-the-path-attribute-2\n\n> If the attribute-value **is empty** or if the first character of the attribute-value is not %x2F (\"/\")... Let cookie-path be the default-path.\n\nSo I think Chrome's behavior is actually correct here.\n\nThe Cookie Store API spec should not instruct callers to reject cookies whose Path string is empty, that seems like a spec bug.\n\n",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
    "reactions": {
