    "created_at": "2025-07-02T06:41:45Z",
    "updated_at": "2025-07-02T06:41:45Z",
    "body": "If we are to take that literally it would mean that we'd also have to treat an input of \"`foo`\" as meaning the URL's path.\n\nIn my mind the API is quite distinct from the parser, but I'm okay on aligning with Chrome and special casing the empty string as that's probably the path of least resistance.\n\n(Note that we also still have #223 on paths.)",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
